<title>CHINA: China bank in 1.93 bln yuan loans to power plant.</title>
<headline>China bank in 1.93 bln yuan loans to power plant.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's State Development Bank (SDB) has extended 1.93 billion yuan ($233 million) in loans to a power plant in southwestern Sichuan province, the Financial News said on Friday.</p>
<p>The Agricultural Bank of China signed an agreement on Thursday to act as agent for the SDB to lend on the credit and would also extend 600 million in loans to the Sichuan Guangan power plant, it said.</p>
<p>The Sichuan Guangan power plant, with 3.24 billion yuan investment in its first phase, would have a total designed installed capacity of 2,400 megawatts, it said but gave no further details.</p>
<p>($1.0 = 8.3 yuan)</p>
<p>-- Beijing Newsroom (8610) 6532 1921</p>
</text>
